    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: First-Time Visitors Pickup Planning</h1>
    <p>Pickup day sets the tone for the whole rental, and a little planning turns it from a queue-and-paperwork errand into the calm start of a good week. This guide is about planning the visit itself: when to come, what the location means for your first ride, what to bring, and how to leave the shop with a machine you know and a plan you believe in. Our shop is at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open 09:00&ndash;21:00 daily, and every recommendation below starts from that verified address.</p>
    <p>This page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> series for first-time visitors. The bike-choice and paperwork articles in the same series cover their own questions, the verified rates are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, and the general rental questions live on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page. Nothing here promises delivery or pickup arrangements; those, where they exist, are confirmed directly with us at booking.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Where we are and what that means</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">When to come: timing the pickup</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">What to bring and what to leave behind</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The first ride: from Long Bien into the city</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Planning the machine handover</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-6">If plans change before or after pickup</a></li>
